== how much an ADJACENT flag is worth ==
   Only the industrial videos carry filename dates, so they are the only
   place the numbering can be calibrated against a known date. Two facts,
   pulling in opposite directions:

   C numbering RESETS. 2019_08_19_C0001_5319_phantom and
   2019_11_14_C0001_3922_matrice share the token C0001 yet carry dates 2019-08-19 and 2019-11-14,
   87 days apart. Equal numbers do not imply one occasion.

   C numbering PERSISTS across outings. 2019_08_19_C0001_5319_phantom
   and 2019_09_02_C0002_2527_inspire are 1 apart in
   numbering yet carry dates 2019-08-19 and 2019-09-02, 14 days apart.
   A gap of 1 therefore spans more than one occasion here.

   GOPR numbering PERSISTS across outings. 2019_08_19_GOPR5869_1530_phantom
   and 2019_09_02_GOPR5871_1058_solo are 2 apart in
   numbering yet carry dates 2019-08-19 and 2019-09-02, 14 days apart.
   A gap of 2 therefore spans more than one occasion here.

   Taken together: a small numbering gap is CONSISTENT with one occasion and
   does not establish it, and the meadow and fisheye videos carry no date at
   all against which to check. The flag marks what the disk cannot separate,
   not what it joins.

== one caveat on the fisheye numbering ==
   gopro_000 to gopro_008 are dataset-assigned names. No committed artefact
   records whether that order reflects camera recording order, so the
   ADJACENT flag on gopro_004 and gopro_005 rests on an ordering whose
   provenance is not established. reports/gopro_continuity_findings.md and
   reports/fisheye_session/FINDINGS.md carry what has been measured on that pair.

